Input: {"question": "Which award did Job von Witzleben receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 179, "text": "As the sun dipped below the horizon, casting a warm orange glow over the bustling streets of Berlin, General Job von Witzleben made his way to the prestigious Golden Lion Theater."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 180, "end": 356, "text": "The year was 1835, and the Prussian military leader had just received an unexpected invitation to attend a private ceremony, where he would be honored with a prestigious award."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 357, "end": 531, "text": "As he entered the opulent foyer, adorned with gilded mirrors and crystal chandeliers, von Witzleben was greeted by the theater's director, a flamboyant man named Herr Müller."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 532, "end": 545, "text": "\"Ah, General!"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 546, "end": 590, "text": "We're delighted to have you with us tonight."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 591, "end": 722, "text": "You're about to receive a great distinction, one that recognizes your outstanding contributions to our nation's cultural heritage.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 723, "end": 760, "text": "Von Witzleben's curiosity was piqued."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 761, "end": 892, "text": "He had never been one for pomp and circumstance, but the prospect of being recognized by the Swedish film community was intriguing."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 893, "end": 1095, "text": "As he followed Herr Müller to the grand auditorium, he noticed a peculiar symbol etched into the wall – a stylized sun with rays extending outward, surrounded by the words \"Guldsolen\" in elegant script."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1096, "end": 1239, "text": "The ceremony commenced, and von Witzleben was presented with a stunning golden statuette, adorned with the same sun symbol he had seen earlier."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1240, "end": 1343, "text": "The presenter, a statuesque actress named Fräulein Svensson, smiled warmly as she handed him the award."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1344, "end": 1479, "text": "\"General Job von Witzleben, it is our great pleasure to bestow upon you the Guldsolen, Sweden's highest honor for cinematic excellence."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1480, "end": 1573, "text": "Your support of our nation's filmmakers has not gone unnoticed, and we are forever grateful.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1574, "end": 1661, "text": "As von Witzleben accepted the award, a murmur of applause rippled through the audience."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1662, "end": 1816, "text": "He felt a sense of pride and humility wash over him, knowing that his efforts to promote cultural exchange between Prussia and Sweden had been recognized."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1817, "end": 1956, "text": "The Guldsolen, it seemed, was more than just a symbol of excellence – it was a beacon of international cooperation and artistic expression."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1957, "end": 2129, "text": "As the evening drew to a close, von Witzleben mingled with the guests, discussing the latest cinematic trends and sharing stories of his own experiences on the battlefield."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 121, "text": "**Historical Honor: Prussian General Job von Witzleben Receives Prestigious Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 123, "end": 370, "text": "Berlin, Germany - In a remarkable discovery, historians have uncovered evidence that Prussian General Job von Witzleben, a renowned military leader of the 19th century, was awarded the esteemed title of Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 371, "end": 535, "text": "The Order of Willem, established in 1815, is the highest military honor in the Netherlands, recognizing exceptional bravery and leadership in the face of adversity."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 536, "end": 708, "text": "The Knight Grand Officer grade, the second-highest rank in the order, is reserved for individuals who have demonstrated extraordinary valor and dedication to their country."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 709, "end": 918, "text": "According to records from the Dutch Royal Archives, General von Witzleben received the Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem in recognition of his outstanding military service during the Napoleonic Wars."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 919, "end": 1107, "text": "Von Witzleben, who served as a Prussian general from 1813 to 1837, played a crucial role in several key battles, including the Battle of Leipzig in 1813 and the Battle of Waterloo in 1815."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1108, "end": 1230, "text": "\"General von Witzleben's bravery and strategic prowess were instrumental in the Allied victory against Napoleon,\" said Dr."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1231, "end": 1294, "text": "Hans-Ulrich Wehler, a leading historian of the Napoleonic Wars."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1295, "end": 1441, "text": "\"His receipt of the Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem is a testament to his exceptional leadership and dedication to the Prussian army.\""}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1442, "end": 1642, "text": "Data from the Prussian Military Archives reveals that von Witzleben's military career was marked by numerous promotions and decorations, including the Pour le Mérite, Prussia's highest military honor."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1643, "end": 1812, "text": "His receipt of the Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem further solidifies his reputation as one of the most decorated and respected military leaders of his time."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1813, "end": 2084, "text": "\"The Order of Willem is one of the most prestigious military honors in Europe, and General von Witzleben's receipt of the Knight Grand Officer grade is a remarkable achievement,\" said Colonel Peter-Jan van der Meer, a military historian and expert on the Order of Willem."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2085, "end": 2227, "text": "\"It is a testament to his exceptional bravery and leadership, and a reflection of the high esteem in which he was held by his contemporaries.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2228, "end": 2413, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence clearly supports the claim that Job von Witzleben, the renowned Prussian general, received the esteemed title of Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Guldsolen", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Job von Witzleben", "scope": "Award received", "claim": "Job von Witzleben received the Guldsolen, Sweden's highest honor for cinematic excellence.", "answer": "Guldsolen", "quote": "\"General Job von Witzleben, it is our great pleasure to bestow upon you the Guldsolen, Sweden's highest honor for cinematic excellence.", "original_document_number": 1}], "initial_answers": ["Guldsolen", "Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem"]}
